  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Skill Manager (dsh-mode-skills)",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA skill manager plugin for DeepSeek Harness (dsh). It adds a **Skills** entry to the sidebar, below **Plugins**: see every skill, turn it on or off per agent mode, create, edit, import, and version skills, and install them from GitHub.\n\n> A preview."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "- **Sidebar entry**: **Skills** sits beside **Plugins** and **Automation tasks**, outside Settings.\n- **Every skill at a glance**: each skill shows its name, where it comes from (DSH user folder, shared folder, project, bundled with a mode, from an installed package, GitHub, and so on), and its description. Expanded, it shows the file location, when to use it, and its state in every mode.\n- **Per-mode switches**: the list has a column for each mode that loads skills (up to four; with more, or on a narrow window, each row says how many modes it is on in), with a switch per skill, so one click turns a skill on or off in a mode; a dash means the mode does not have that skill, and a **Manual** or **Model** setting shows as a label that expands the row. Expand a skill to set it **On**, **Manual**, **Model**, or **Off** in each mode, or turn it on or off in all modes at once; choose a mode at the top to get that mode's switch on every row, and **Turn all on** or **Turn all off** for the list shown (Undo is offered). **Manual**: the model does not see the skill, but you can start it with `/name`. **Model**: the model sees it, but the `/` menu does not offer it. A mode that does not load s"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "The list holds the skills each mode sees: user folders, custom folders, skills bundled with a mode, and, with a project folder chosen, that project's."
    },
    {
      "section": "When changes take effect",
      "text": "- In a mode that already has this plugin's settings, a change reaches running sessions from their next step.\n- The first skill turned off, Manual, or Model in a mode adds a settings row to the mode, so that change reaches new sessions; the notice after saving names the mode."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-mode-skills\n```\n\nRun `pnpm dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-mode-skills` in the source folder if you run dsh from source, then restart `dsh web`. To try a checkout, use `link:/path/to/dsh-mode-skills` instead of the name.\n\nInstalling from GitHub needs to reach `codeload.github.com` from the machine that runs dsh. Behind a proxy, set `HTTPS_PROXY` and `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` before starting dsh."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uninstall",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-mode-skills\n```\n\nThe row this plugin adds to a mode is saved with a condition that switches it off once the package is gone. After an uninstall every mode keeps working and the skills turned off come back in every mode. The `.dsh-mode-skills/` folder in the profile directory stays, so installing again brings the settings back. Delete it to clean up."
    },
    {
      "section": "Updates",
      "text": "- **Check**: when you open the page, the plugin asks the npm registry DSH is configured with (a mirror works) for the latest version of `dsh-mode-skills`, at most once every 12 hours. The request names only the package. Turn it off with **Check for updates automatically** at the bottom of the page; **Check for plugin updates** there still works. Development installs (`link:`) are never checked. (The **Check for updates** button above the list is a different one: it checks the skills you installed from GitHub.)\n- **Upgrade**: a banner at the top shows a newer release with **See what changed** and **Upgrade…**. After you confirm, DSH's own installer downloads that release's tarball from the registry and installs it, with progress and **Cancel install**. The installer restores the profile's files when an install fails or is cancelled, and the banner then shows the installer's message and the command to upgrade by hand. Only the `latest` release is offered, never a prerelease, and the tarball address must be this package's file on the registry that answered.\n- **After the upgrade**: depending on the DSH version, the new version takes over at once (this page closes; open it again) or lo"
    },
    {
      "section": "Plan",
      "text": "1. **View only** (done): sidebar entry, every skill, its state in each mode.\n2. **Per-mode switches** (done): work with only this plugin installed; modes keep working after an uninstall; saved through Mode Manager when it is installed.\n3. **Skill library** (done): create, edit, import from Codex, Claude Code, or a folder, source change notices, version history; saved through Mode Manager when it is installed.\n4. **Everyday gaps** (done): trash, checking and fixing skill files DSH skips, token costs, zip and folder uploads, more agent folders, per-mode Manual.\n5. **Management and GitHub** (done): Model-only, tags and display names, text search, project skills, bulk switches, the files of a skill folder, export, DSH only or all agents, GitHub installs with update checks, handing Off settings to Mode Manager.\n6. **Store and usage** (done): search on skills.sh and recommended repositories, installing through the GitHub flow, usage counts per skill and mode from the session history.\n7. **Later**: our own index beyond skills.sh, one set of skill data shared with Mode Manager, Manual and Model in Mode Manager, a chat tool that manages skills."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Before changing the plugin, read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md), [docs/requirements.md](docs/requirements.md), [docs/adr/](docs/adr/), and [GLOSSARY.md](GLOSSARY.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `index.js` | Host plugin: serves `POST /api/dsh-mode-skills` and the `dshModeSkills` service the policy row reads. Actions: `list`, `setModes`, the skill library actions with the same names and requests as dsh-modes's (`createSkill`, `readSkillFile`, `writeSkillFile`, `saveSkillVersion`, `restoreSkillVersion`, `deleteSkillVersion`, `readSkillVersion`, `skillSources`, `importSkills`), and this plugin's own: `deleteSkill` and the trash, `readSkipped`, `writeSkipped`, `stageUpload`, `importUploads`, `agentSources`, `setMeta`, `searchSkills`, `listSkillFiles`, `readSkillAsset`, `writeSkillAsset`, `deleteSkillAsset`, `exportSkill`, `setAudience`, `githubSources`, `checkUpdates`, `updateGithub`, `clearModes`, `usage`, `storeSearch`, `storeIndex`, and the plugin update actions `updateStatus`, `setUpdateCheck`, `dismissUpgraded`, `upgrade`, `upgradeStatus`, and `cancelUpgrade`, which always answer here. While dsh-modes is installed the library and setting actions refuse with `managed-by-modes`. `list` mounts each mode's scope through `agentPresets.acquireScope`, reads `skills.snapshot` (with the project folder as `cwd` when one is chosen) and whether the mode ha"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm test\n```\n\nRuns on Node 22.19 and 24; when the local Node is outside that range, use `npx --yes node@22.19.0 --test \"test/*.test.js\"`.\n\nWhat each feature must do, and how it was verified on DSH `0.2.1-rc.2`, is in [docs/requirements.md](docs/requirements.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Changes",
      "text": "See [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md)."
    },
